  "limitations": [
    "The fixture is 4 Python files and 7 entities; this validates first-run mechanics, not large-repository performance.",
    "The Claude Code and Codex client binaries were not installed, so --write client execution was not run; the exact commands and TOML/JSON snippets were rendered, and the MCP handshake was executed directly.",
    "The release zip was not rebuilt with the M1 binaries; tooling/test_release.py now includes an installed-bundle init handshake, but that packaging path was not re-run in this slice.",
    "Direct archmeld index re-runs on identical bytes still use a new run id and can hit the external-entity payload conflict; archmeld init avoids this by reusing a clean snapshot. Track as a follow-up for the low-level index path.",
    "brief is a deterministic composition of status and static review. It does not execute tests, synthesize architecture, or infer new calls; candidate relations remain candidate and verification is not_run.",
    "M3 commit supervision and M4 scoped multi-agent authority are not part of M1.",
    "The local GNU toolchain now has the rust-analyzer component because the pre-existing language_rename_apply acceptance test resolves it from the toolchain bin; this is a test-environment change, not a product dependency."
  ]
